#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Example: Physics 🚀]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Inverse functions can be used to find initial conditions]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Example: Finding initial velocity given final velocity and time]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[$ v_f = v_i + at $]
#v(20pt)
#only("4-")[$ v_i = v_f - at $]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("In physics, inverse functions can be used to find initial conditions.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("For example, if you know the final velocity of an object and the time taken, you can use the inverse function to find the initial velocity.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("The equation 'v sub f equals v sub i plus a t' represents the relationship between initial velocity, final velocity, acceleration, and time.")
]
#only("4")[
#voiceover("By rearranging the equation, we get 'v sub i equals v sub f minus a t', which is the inverse function used to find the initial velocity.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Example: Economics 📈]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Composite functions can model supply and demand relationships]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Example: Demand as a function of price, which is a function of supply]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[$ D(P(S)) $]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("In economics, composite functions can be used to model supply and demand relationships.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("For instance, demand can be expressed as a function of price, which in turn is a function of supply.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("This composite function is written as 'D of P of S', where D represents demand, P represents price, and S represents supply.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Example: Biology 🌿]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Composite functions can model population dynamics]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Example: Population size as a function of food supply, which is a function of environmental factors]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[$ P(F(E)) $]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("In biology, composite functions can be used to model population dynamics.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("For example, population size can be modeled as a function of food supply, which itself is a function of environmental factors.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("This composite function is written as 'P of F of E', where P represents population size, F represents food supply, and E represents environmental factors.")
]
]

